From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:50:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Review: only armed ranks are asked for a stack; a
 Python launcher is left out; a silent rank is named

- The dump request went to every descendant of the job. mpirun forwards
  SIGUSR1 to its ranks, so each rank dumped twice per sample. Only processes
  this module armed (those with a stack file, the newest per pid) are asked.
- A Python driver that starts its ranks was armed, asked and counted, and
  could be named as the rank somewhere the others are not. An armed process
  with an armed descendant of a different rank is a launcher, and is neither
  asked nor counted. A rank's own helpers inherit its rank variable, so a rank
  with a compile running is still asked.
- The report names each asked rank whose stack file stayed empty.

test_0063: a Python driver's ranks are dumped and the driver leaves no file;
a forwarding launcher (a shell trapping SIGUSR1, standing in for mpirun)
gets its rank two dumps, not four; the silent rank is named. All three fail
before this change.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
